</table></td></tr></table></body></html>$h$, $t$VANTIX BIO

Before you trust any COA

A certificate is easy to fake. A batch you can check is not.

Hello, almost every peptide site says “tested.” What matters is whether you can confirm it yourself, without taking the seller’s word for it.
So instead of telling you our results are good, here are two short reads that show you how to judge any report, ours included.
Read this first
A real report, line by line
An actual third-party lab report, annotated field by field, including the awkward parts: a quantity above the label amount, and a sample name that did not match.
Read the walkthrough → (https://vantixbio.com/blog/real-janoshik-coa-walkthrough.html?utm_source=email&utm_medium=retention&utm_campaign=welcome-d3)
Then keep this
Five red flags in any peptide COA
What to look for on reports from any seller, and the five-minute check to run before you buy.
See the red flags → (https://vantixbio.com/blog/5-red-flags-fake-peptide-coas.html?utm_source=email&utm_medium=retention&utm_campaign=welcome-d3)
When you are ready to order: orders typically ship within one business day, most arrive within about a week, and your first-order code WELCOME15 takes 15% off. Questions about a report? Reply and ask.
Open the verification portal (https://vantixbio.com/verify.html?utm_source=email&utm_medium=retention&utm_campaign=welcome-d3)  ·  Visit the shop (https://vantixbio.com/shop.html?utm_source=email&utm_medium=retention&utm_campaign=welcome-d3)

For laboratory research use only. Not for human consumption.
Vantix Bio, PO Box 389, Santa Cruz, CA 95061
You are receiving this because you signed up at vantixbio.com. Unsubscribe (https://vantixbio.com/unsubscribe.html#e={{email}})
$t$),
